  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UN Kenya Joint Program on Youth Skills, Employability and Civic Engagement</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Joint Programme (JP) aims to increase access to employment and entrepreneurship opportunities for youth in Kenya and enhance their voice and agency in governance and development processes. It prioritizes young women, young persons with disability, those in ASAL counties and informal urban settlements, who are at risk of being left behind. The JP will be implemented in five counties namely: Nairobi, Mombasa, Kisumu, Turkana and Isiolo.</narrative>
  </description>
